Paul of Tarsus: On the Roads of Rome
Copyright (c) 2026 Marco Warm. All rights reserved.

The source code of this game is public so that it can be read, played and
improved together. It is not open source. "The game" below means everything in
this repository: the code, the artwork and music it paints and synthesizes,
the text in every language, and the documentation.

1. What you may do

   a. Play. You may play the game at its official address,
      https://paul-of-tarsus.theunknownones.net/, install it as an app from
      there, and download an unchanged copy to play on your own devices. All
      of this is free of charge.

   b. Read. You may read the source code and the documentation.

   c. Propose changes. You may copy the game and change it only to prepare a
      change that you propose to the official repository,
      https://github.com/MarcusCalidus/paul-of-tarsus, as a pull request. This
      includes a fork on GitHub and running your changed copy on your own
      computer to test it. A change is proposed under the rules in
      CONTRIBUTING.md.

   d. Change your own copy. You may change a copy for your own private use,
      for example for your family or to try out an idea, as long as you do
      not pass it on or put it online.

   e. Link. You are welcome to share links to the official address and to the
      official repository.

2. What you may not do

   Anything not allowed in section 1 needs the written permission of the
   copyright holder. In particular, you may not:

   a. publish, host or pass on a copy of the game, changed or unchanged,
      anywhere other than as described in section 1. A fork is only a
      place to prepare a pull request: it must not be published as a
      website, for example with GitHub Pages;
   b. publish a changed version of the game, or a game built from its code,
      art, music or text;
   c. use the game or any part of it commercially: sell it, charge for it,
      show advertising with it, or include it in a paid product or service;
   d. use the name "Paul of Tarsus" for another game, or present a copy or a
      changed version as the official game.

3. Contributions

   When you propose a change (a pull request, a patch, a translation, a text or
   any other contribution), you grant Marco Warm a worldwide, free of charge,
   perpetual and irrevocable right to use, change, publish and sublicense it,
   as part of the game or otherwise, under these terms or any other license he
   chooses. You confirm that the contribution is your own work, or that you
   have the right to grant this, and that it contains no material that
   CONTRIBUTING.md forbids. Contributors are named in the credits on request.

